msgid ""
"The broadcasted object makes 5 (since the x-grid has 5 points) identical "
"copies of the whole variable ``c_s`` to give an object with size 5x3=15. In "
"the resulting vector, the first 3 entries correspond to the 3 points in the "
"r-domain at the first x-grid point (where c_s varies in r), the next 3 "
"entries correspond to the next 3 points in the r-domain at the second x-grid "
"point (where c_s varies in r), etc"
